{
  "case_id": "2008-07-773",
  "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case poses two substantive issues:\nFirst, whether section 4 of the Federal Arbitration Act impliedly repeals section 1331's \"well-pleaded complaint\" requirement? Only if it does can a district court look through a petition to compel arbitration that itself contains no Federal question to ground Federal subject matter jurisdiction on a Federal question lurking somewhere in the dispute sought to be arbitrated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument next in Vaden v. Discover Bank. Mr. Ortiz."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Your Honors, the ordinary, the original meaning of section 4, the structure of the overall Federal Arbitration Act, and the purposes of the Federal Arbitration Act all militate strongly in favor of the Petitioner's view of subject matter jurisdiction here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Ortiz, why isn't section 2 of the Arbitration Act sufficient to take care of the ouster doctrine, whatever may have been left of it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: I'm just not getting the -- I have never understood this argument and I still don't understand it now. What is it in the text of section 2 that would seem to leave it inadequate to touch equity as well as law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: I hate to interrupt you here, but would you explain why the words \"save for such agreement\" cut back on the jurisdiction? I didn't quite understand your point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is Petitioner's contention that section 4 has no independent look-through force. To the extent that look through is appropriate, it is because it is appropriate under section 1332, itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "implication of taking the kind of look-through theory that Respondents are arguing for in this case"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you would say, well, the dispute is between A and B and C; and so you would be depriving A of their right to frame their own complaint in a way that doesn't create Federal jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 4 is the only section of the arbitration -- in the Federal Arbitration Act that has the critical \"save for such\" language"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Two law professors (amici)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the closest Respondent comes to sort of explaining this or trying to jump or leap over this gap, are two amici, two law professors, who argue that this Court should find jurisdiction, subject matter jurisdiction under sections 7, 9, 10 and 11 as an emanation from sections 3 and 4, only one of which actually has the necessary \"save for\" language."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. PHILLIPS",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "made an allegation here that the subject matter of this dispute arises under Federal law"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Speaking of gymnastics, can I ask you if you had foreseen this problem, could you have brought a declaratory judgment action to establish that your Federal claim --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Right. Well, that's exactly what the Eleventh Circuit held."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Is the State court suit still pending?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: The State court has stayed its hand pending the outcome of the Federal litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: That's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is the Petitioner's -- I'm sorry I didn't get a chance to ask the Petitioner -- is the Petitioner's argument for a limited look through compromised in any way by the Beneficial Bank case which allows removal if there is a Federal defense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Because I think -- I think the reference in the statute to controversy clearly envisions the underlying dispute between the parties, because it's not just the arbitration agreement and it's not even just the controversy; it's the subject matter of the controversy, and you compare that to section 2 and it's clear that what the Congress has in mind there is the underlying dispute between the parties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: That isn't quite true, because here there is a definition in the Federal claim"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-773",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f8d9b98a34ac9ce48783cd2941e7b1e2bacfeb69be8055c0292a263b0c512fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f8d9b98a34a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
